# Keep line endings stable in the repository regardless of who commits.
#
# Without this, files written on Linux (LF) and committed from Windows (CRLF)
# show up as whole-file diffs the next time either side touches them. Storing
# LF and letting Git convert on checkout keeps the history readable.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and generated files Git should never try to normalise.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
